  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACCORD:Enhancing Responses for Renewed Opportunities for Conflict Prevention &amp; Peacebuilding in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The African Centre for the Constructive Resolution of Disputes (ACCORD) will undertake a series of activities and dialogues to unpack the contemporary challenges to multilateralism and discuss opportunities for a reinvigoration of conflict prevention and peacebuilding in Africa.

These activities and dialogues align with Denmark&#x2019;s United Nations Security Council (UNSC) elected term of 2025-2026. Denmark&apos;s term will focuses on equality, security and action. Denmark will use the membership opportunity to:
&#x2022; Prioritise international law and a more effective and representative Security Council;
&#x2022; Look into conflict responses and prevention fit for new realities;
&#x2022; Focus on climate peace and security; and
&#x2022; Women, peace and security.

 ACCORD proposes to use the SDG funds available via the Danish Embassy for the following:
&#x2022; Seminar focused on Prioritising Equality, Security and Action with African countries;
&#x2022; Roundtable/Webinar on Climate, Peace &amp; Livelihoods in the SADC region linked to the African Common
  Position on Climate Change;
&#x2022; Africa Consultation on the 2025 UN Peacebuilding Architecture Review and SG Peacebuilding Report;
&#x2022; WPS Lessons Learned (UN Resolution 1325 25th anniversary) reflections on prevention of, and
    accountability for conflict related sexual violence.</narrative>
  </description>
